  "id": "COMPOUND:14268 - PROTEIN:4647",
  "verbalization": "Benzocaine exhibits a strong, consistent relationship with Calcium/calmodulin-dependent protein kinase kinase 1 (CaMKK1) through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that benzocaine acts as a target of multiple molecular entities, which in turn target CaMKK1. Specifically, benzocaine is linked to Geminin, a protein that is itself a target of a complex compound with a known structure, and this compound is also a target of CaMKK1. Similarly, benzocaine is associated with Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1, which is also a target of the same complex compound, and this compound again targets CaMKK1. Additionally, benzocaine is connected to Dual specificity protein kinase CLK2, which is also a target of the same complex compound and ultimately targets CaMKK1.\n\nThe mechanism appears to involve a chain of molecular interactions where benzocaine serves as a substrate or target of a complex compound that, in turn, targets CaMKK1. This suggests that the interaction between benzocaine and CaMKK1 is mediated through a shared intermediate, which is a complex compound with a well-defined structure. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between benzocaine and CaMKK1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways converging on CaMKK1 indicates a potential role in downstream signaling processes, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
